A||||9||GodSend||Help with o-ring - Need to get this back together before noon||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||10-20-2001||10:37 AM||||Hey guys, really quick and weasy question<P>I have my dist out,  I could not find the old o-ring, or where to put the new one.<P>I got the oring straight from Pontiac, part # 10477565.  It is brown in color and large enough to easily fit over my thumb.<P>Heres the problem.  It is only large enough to fit over the first inch and a half of the dist. shaft.  It can not make it over the "geared" section.<P>I was under the impression that it would sit right underneath the last ridge on the side of the engine block.<P>Please help, I only have an hour and a half to get this baby back together||||reg||1
Z||000001||William Federle||10-20-2001||10:57 AM||||I replaced mine about 1.5 yrs ago, but I think I remember it going into the groove just under the flange that is showing on the outside after you put the distributer back in. If there is nothing there now, it must have come off when you pulled the distributer out. (mine disintegrated when I tried to pull it out of its groove after getting the distributer out.<P>    Assuming they gave you the correct o-ring at the pontiac dealer, lube it with motor oil and stretch it over the various diameters until you get to the groove it goes in.<P>Good luck.<p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-20-2001||10:59 AM||||A bit of engine oil should do it for you. Lube it up and slip it on over, it will stretch a little for you as well when you make it to the groove. That will also assist you on the installation of the distributor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||10-20-2001||11:21 AM||||I did mine, had the same problem, it's just REALLY FRIGGEN TIGHT.  As for the old one it just fell apart on me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GodSend||10-20-2001||12:02 PM||||Thanks guys.. I got it on, but I am having problems getting the dist back in.<P>I can get it so the shaft is almost on (needs about maybe .5 cms more) - the marks I made almost line up (hopefully they will shift a tiny bit more then I get the thing on).<P>I lubed it up real good (no jokes please!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) but I can't seem to get that last little bit down.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||10-20-2001||12:38 PM||||Since you now have it properly lubed, start with the hold down clamped in place, start screwing in the bolt so you won't fall out.<P>Get in there real good, but not yet 'penetrated' to the point that with a little force your able to 'rotate' just a bit.     <BR>Adjust your timing, and adjust your 'rotation', till it feels good!<BR>When your all set and you see in the hole that your ready, 'Drive it home and screw it'!<BR>Feels good!||||reg||1
Z||000006||William Federle||10-20-2001||02:27 PM||||I'll bet you didn't know that Fieros could be that exciting.||||reg||1
